# Build context is the repo root; only server/ and my-react-app/ are copied.
#
# .env is excluded on purpose: secrets belong to the container's environment
# (compose reads deploy/.env), not to an image layer that anyone who can pull
# the image can read back out.
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

my-react-app/dist
my-react-app/dev-dist
my-react-app/.vite
my-react-app/node_modules/.vite*
server/uploads

certs/
.git/
docs/
scripts/
**/*.log
**/*.err
_*.log
_*.err
_*.bak
*.md
*.bat
*.ps1
*.txt

# Ad-hoc scratch that must never reach a distributable artifact. `COPY server/ ./`
# takes whatever is in the directory, so a diagnostic dump written next to the code
# ships inside the image layer. `_profile_oneline.json` is exactly that: a row-for-row
# copy of a live user document (name, email, date of birth, 2FA state). Nothing at
# runtime reads any of these; the server entry point never requires them.
**/_profile*.json
**/_*.json
server/_*.js
server/_*.cjs

# Tests and their harnesses. They connect to databases and hold recorded fixtures;
# none of it is reachable from `index.js`. Migration and diagnostic scripts are
# deliberately NOT listed: an operator may run them with `docker compose exec`,
# and they read their secrets from the environment rather than storing any.
server/Test File/
server/test-*.js
